From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:56:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 180/209] feat(area): polygon shape component

CPolygonShapeComponent is the component form of EditorQt's CShapeObject, minus
everything that was area semantics: a point list in the component's local space,
a Height that extrudes it (0 = infinite in Z, what a legacy shape with
mv_height == 0 means to CArea), a Closed flag, an Offset, and per-face sound
obstruction.

Per decision 03, obstruction lives on the point struct (SPolygonPoint { Vec3
pos; bool obstructSound; }) instead of in a parallel std::vector<bool> the way
legacy does it (ShapeObject.h:246): one point, one flag, so no insert or remove
can desync the two lists. Roof and floor are two members on the component.
The point list is reflected as SPolygonPoints, the GUID + operator== + free
Serialize wrapper a std::vector member needs (research/04 section 5.3, the
CAINavigationMarkupShapeComponent::SShapesArray pattern).

The contract is implemented in full: point-in-polygon on XY plus the height
band for containment (floor = the lowest point's Z, Area.cpp:2298-2302), a
prism signed-distance field for DistanceToHull, ray versus walls and caps,
rejection sampling in the footprint AABB for a random point, the points as the
contour, and listeners with the coarsest EShapeChangeReason a gesture produced.
ENTITY_EVENT_XFORM notifies Transform; an inspector edit notifies Topology when
the point count changed and Geometry otherwise.

EditorHitTest picks the shape by its drawn lines only - footprint, roof ring
and vertical edges - which is what CShapeObject::HitTest does (:1085-1150); the
box's solid fallback would make a large polygon swallow every click inside it.
The geometry it needs is copied into Shapes/ShapeGeometry.h rather than taken
from EditorCommon/Util/Math.h, because an engine module cannot link the editor.

Box and Polygon declare each other incompatible (decision 01: one shape per
entity; the check at EntityObject.cpp:729 is one-directional, so both sides
declare it), and IShapeComponentEdit gains IsContourClosed() at the end of the
interface - the point tool needs it to know which edges exist.

